Create a React single-page web app for finding weekly team meeting times. It should
work like when2meet in "days of the week" mode. The app should allow users to create a new meeting and specify their availability for times on each day of the week. An event creator should be able to share a link to the meeting with others, who can then indicate their availability as well. The app should display a grid showing the availability of all participants, and highlight the times when everyone is Available.

Features: 
Grabbing the url, getting a custom short hashed url, to share
Easier way to see who responded and who did not
Vertical table where you can drag or click cells to select them
Prioritize times by clicking for a different pen color for Not Preferred or Available, with an empty cell representing Not Available
Cells are in 15 minute intervals

Input Start/End Dates or format days of the week MTuWThFSaSu

Input Time start and Time End

Input Meeting details in a form, like length of time, location, description, etc.
	Once meeting time is picked, can share calendar.ics or download it

Output the top X (X can be picked, like 3 or 5) meeting times along with a similar When2Meet heatmap next to it
Making sure algorithm for top times prioritizes total number of people who can make at least part of the meeting ahead of people’s priorities
Easier way to see who can make each top X meeting time
Possibility of sending out a poll for selected top 1 out of top X (likely we won’t do)
Select best time out of the output list for calendar.ics


The app should be built using React and TypeScript, and it should use Firebase for
backend services. The app should be hosted on Firebase, using sign-in with Google
for authentication, and storing data in the Firebase Realtime Database. The app
should also include a simple UI for creating and managing meetings, as well as a
grid view for displaying availability.
